                                "sense_id": "3faf958e-e33b-3a86-983f-cd1e6b08488a",
                                "text": "You'll have a nice walk, as the snow is very crup."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ae179d2-bec0-4f0c-a65b-79e9e3720bb3",
                                "sense_id": "3faf958e-e33b-3a86-983f-cd1e6b08488a",
                                "text": "Why now so angry, trow ye? What's the matter, That our Sir James is grown so crup and tatter?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d2c3f20-17a2-4460-bbc4-4a0ee30887e8",
                                "sense_id": "3faf958e-e33b-3a86-983f-cd1e6b08488a",
                                "text": "[…] and care must be had to rost him so leasurely, that he neither burn, nor continue raw: for when the skin seems crup, it is a sign all is rosted, and the Polenta is taken away."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a09e2ba-7e1b-4261-91a1-bae25e169e07",
                                "sense_id": "3faf958e-e33b-3a86-983f-cd1e6b08488a",
                                "text": "He was tedious crup with me."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
